{{also|half-back}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|half|back}}, in reference to position on the field of play; compare {{m|en|fullback}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|field sports}} Any of various [[position]]s on the [[field of play]] between the [[forward]]s and the [[fullback]]s.
# {{lb|en|field sports}} A [[player]] who occupies one of these positions.
## {{lb|en|American football}} An [[offensive back]] whose primary jobs are to carry the ball on running plays and to serve as a [[receiver]] or [[blocker]] on passing plays.
## {{lb|en|Canadian football}} A [[defensive back]] whose primary jobs are to cover the [[slotback]] on passing plays and prevent running plays from going to the outside.
## {{lb|en|field hockey}} A [[position]] in field hockey, with both [[offensive]] and [[defensive]] roles.
## {{lb|en|Australian Rules}} One of three positions (the [[centre halfback]] and two [[halfback flanker]]s) on the line between the centre line and the fullback line.
## {{lb|en|Rugby}} The player who feeds the ball into the [[scrum]], and [[receive]]s the ball as it [[emerge]]s from the back of the scrum.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To play in the position of halfback.